        "comments": "The McMaster isolate is a strain of H. contortus with no history of exposure to anthelmintics. This strain, originally isolated by researchers at the Commonwealth Scientific Industrial Research Organization (CSIRO), Australia, was isolated prior to the introduction of broad spectrum anthelmintics and has been used routinely as an anthelmintic-susceptible reference strain in anthelmintic resistance studies. Female worms of the McMaster strain are all of the linguiform morphological type. This strain has been routinely maintained in various laboratories by serial passage in sheep.",
